@startuml
autonumber
skinparam Style strictuml
skinparam MaxMessageSize 250
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20

actor "User A" as UA
actor "User B" as UB
participant "Nginx" as NX
box "API Gateway (Orchestrator)" #LightYellow
    participant "Gateway A" as GWA
    participant "Gateway B" as GWB
end box
participant "Matching Service" as MS
participant "Question Service" as QS
participant "Collab Service\n(Socket.IO)" as Collab
database "Redis (Pub/Sub & State)" as RD

== Phase 1: Generic Matching ==

UA -> NX: POST /api/matching/find-pair (criteria_1_opts, criteria_2_opts, JWT)
NX -> GWA: Forward Request
GWA -> GWA: Auth: Verify JWT A
GWA -> MS: POST /find-pair (uid_A, criteria_1_opts, criteria_2_opts)

... Both users queue ...

MS -> RD: PUBLISH match_events {uid_A, uid_B, crit_1, crit_2}

== Phase 2: Distributed Session Initialization ==

RD -->> GWA: [Message Received]
RD -->> GWB: [Message Received]

GWA -> GWA: Generate sessionId_A
GWB -> GWB: Generate sessionId_B

note over GWA, GWB: Atomic Race: The first sessionId to reach Redis becomes the shared session ID, and the Gateway that obtains the lock becomes the leader.

GWA -> RD: SETNX lock:match:A:B sessionId_A
GWB -> RD: SETNX lock:match:A:B sessionId_B

RD --> GWA: 1 (Leader)
RD --> GWB: 0 (Follower)

group Leader Logic (GWA)
    GWA -> QS: GET /questions?topic=crit_1&diff=crit_2
    QS --> GWA: {qid: "q_101", ...}
    GWA -> RD: SET session:sessionId_A:meta {"users": ["A", "B"], "qid": "q_101"}
    GWA -> RD: SET session:sessionId_A:editor {"code": "", "version": 0}
    GWA -->> UA: [Notify] Match Found! {sessionId: sessionId_A}
end

group Follower Logic (GWB)
    GWB -> RD: GET lock:match:A:B
    RD --> GWB: sessionId_A (Follower retrieves winning ID)
    GWB -> RD: WAIT/POLL for session:sessionId_A:meta
    GWB -->> UB: [Notify] Match Found! {sessionId: sessionId_A}
end

== Phase 3: Ticket Acquisition & WebSocket Connection ==

UA -> NX: POST /api/collab/join (JWT, sessionId_A)
NX -> GWA: Forward (strip /api)
GWA -> GWA: Verify JWT, check session membership
GWA -> RD: SET ticket:UUID {uid_A, sessionId_A} EX 60
GWA --> UA: { ticket: "UUID_1" }

UA -> NX: WS /socket.io/?ticket=UUID_1
NX -> Collab: Proxy Upgrade (plain passthrough)
Collab -> RD: GETDEL ticket:UUID_1
RD --> Collab: {uid_A, sessionId_A}
Collab -> Collab: Attach userId & sessionId to socket
Collab --> UA: HTTP 101 (WebSocket established)

note over NX, Collab
  Ticket validation happens in the collab service
  Socket.IO middleware, not via nginx auth_request.
  One ticket per connection (editor + chat = 2 tickets).
end note

== Phase 4: Real-time Collaboration ==

UA -> Collab: /editor — yjs-update (Yjs binary delta)
Collab -> RD: RPUSH session:sessionId_A:ydoc (base64)
Collab -> RD: SET session:sessionId_A:finalCode (plaintext)
Collab -> UB: Broadcast yjs-update

UA -> Collab: /chat — send-message ("Hello!")
Collab -> RD: RPUSH session:sessionId_A:chat (JSON, trim to 500)
Collab -> UB: Broadcast receive-message

note over Collab
  /editor and /chat are separate Socket.IO namespaces.
  Each requires its own ticket for connection.
  Yjs updates use CRDT for conflict-free merging.
end note
@enduml
